findings = [
 {
  "ref": "new",
  "title": "The deployed PositionManager refuses to mint claims, so a position with one currency that cannot leave the PoolManager closes only by forfeiting that side or by placing it in a new position, and the published SDK builds neither call",
  "chainIds": ALL,
  "lens": "L3",
  "assumptions": ["A4", "A6"],
  "effect": "freeze",
  "actor": "unprivileged",
  "severity": "medium",
  "difference": "Several of the 21 networks hold pooled tokens that refuse a transfer from the PoolManager address under a rule that Ethereum pools rarely meet. ViciCoin on Polygon counts every PoolManager transfer against a daily net outflow limit that any account can use up (F-072). G$ on Celo blocks the PoolManager as sender (F-056). Ten wrapped stock tokens on Monad can be paused by a two signature Safe (F-061). TIP-20 tokens on Tempo carry transfer policies set by their issuers. The PoolManager core can still pay such a currency out as an ERC-6909 claim, but the PositionManager that holds the positions of ordinary users does not expose that route on any of the 21 networks.",
  "mechanism": "1. A position made through the PositionManager belongs to the PositionManager inside the PoolManager, so its owner can act only through PositionManager.modifyLiquidities and the action list of _handleAction. 2. A removal creates a positive delta in both currencies for the PositionManager. Every delta must be zero when unlock returns (src/PoolManager.sol:104-114). 3. TAKE, TAKE_PAIR and CLOSE_CURRENCY end in PoolManager.take, which calls transfer on the token (src/PoolManager.sol:291-297, src/types/Currency.sol:60-86). When the token refuses, the whole call reverts and the other currency stays in the pool as well. 4. Core offers mint(to, id, amount) to turn a positive delta into a claim without touching the token (src/PoolManager.sol:322-329). The PositionManager does not handle action 0x17 (MINT_6909) or 0x18 (BURN_6909). A read-only modifyLiquidities call with action 0x17 reverts with UnsupportedAction(0x17), data 0x5cda29d7 followed by 0x17, on all 21 networks. SWEEP does not help because the tokens never reach the PositionManager. 5. Two sequences succeed in simulation from the position owner. Sequence A is DECREASE_LIQUIDITY or BURN_POSITION, TAKE of the other currency, then CLEAR_OR_TAKE of the blocked currency with amountMax set to the maximum uint256. That calls PoolManager.clear (src/PoolManager.sol:310-319), which erases the delta. The tokens stay in the PoolManager balance with no delta and no claim behind them, so the provider loses that side for good. Sequence B is DECREASE_LIQUIDITY, TAKE of the other currency, MINT_POSITION_FROM_DELTAS (action 0x05) into a range on the side of the current price that holds only the blocked currency, then CLEAR_OR_TAKE for the rounding remainder. The provider leaves with the other currency and a new position that holds the blocked currency. No sequence leaves the provider with an ERC-6909 claim. 6. The v4 SDK that Uniswap publishes for building these calls ends every removal and every fee collection with TAKE_PAIR, and its Actions enum has the lines for MINT_POSITION_FROM_DELTAS and CLEAR_OR_TAKE commented out, so a front end built on it cannot produce sequence A or B. Simulations: Celo position 178 (G$ and cUSD) at block 83,530,712 and Polygon position 60652 (WETH and VCNT) at block 97,817,338 with the tokens as they are today, Monad position 651334 at block 124,698,657 and Arc position 333954 at block 32,722,324 with one currency replaced by reverting code through an eth_call state override. In all four the six sequences that pay or close the blocked side revert, MINT_6909 reverts with UnsupportedAction, and sequences A and B succeed.",
  "impact": "For a user who relies on a front end, a block on one token of a pool also locks the other currency of every position in that pool, although core could release it. On Polygon an ordinary account can cause this at will: F-072 shows that one account can keep the shared ViciCoin allowance of 6 VCNT per day at zero, and 8 of the 15 ViciCoin pools have an open position held through the PositionManager. On Celo 5 of 8 G$ pools have such a position and the standard removal reverts today. On Monad a pause of the wrapped stock tokens would put the USDC side of about 7.9 million dollars of pools (figure from F-061) in the same state. A provider who learns of sequence A loses the blocked side. A provider who uses sequence B keeps it as a range position that converts to the other currency if the price crosses the range. No funds move to the attacker.",
  "preconditions": "A pooled token refuses transfers from the PoolManager. On Polygon any account can bring this about for VCNT by using up the daily allowance. On the other networks it needs the token issuer or its transfer policy. The provider holds the position through the PositionManager and uses a front end that builds removals with TAKE_PAIR. Not confirmed: which calls the hosted Uniswap web application sends for a removal. I read the published SDK, and the application may build its transactions through a server interface whose output I did not capture.",
  "mitigations": "Add MINT_6909 and BURN_6909 handling with the caller as recipient and payer to the PositionManager that ships with this deployment, or publish a documented exit that uses MINT_POSITION_FROM_DELTAS. Front ends can fall back to sequence B when a simulation of TAKE_PAIR fails, and should warn before sequence A. Providers in pools with a token that has issuer controls or a transfer quota can hold positions through their own contract that calls PoolManager.mint for a side that cannot be paid.",
  "coreRefs": ["src/PoolManager.sol:104-114", "src/PoolManager.sol:291-297", "src/PoolManager.sol:310-319", "src/PoolManager.sol:322-329", "src/types/Currency.sol:60-86"],
  "sources": [
   {"url": SRCFY % (1, '0xbD216513d74C8cf14cf4747E6AaA6420FF64ee9e'), "supports": "Verified source of the Ethereum PositionManager (match). src/PositionManager.sol:197-286 lists the handled actions: 0x00 to 0x05, SETTLE_PAIR, TAKE_PAIR, SETTLE, TAKE, CLOSE_CURRENCY, CLEAR_OR_TAKE, SWEEP, WRAP, UNWRAP. Lines 474-484 show _clearOrTake calling poolManager.clear when the credit is at most amountMax. The Actions library defines MINT_6909 as 0x17 and BURN_6909 as 0x18 and the handler has no branch for them."},
   {"url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Uniswap/sdks/main/sdks/v4-sdk/src/PositionManager.ts", "supports": "removeCallParameters (lines 334-391) encodes BURN_POSITION or DECREASE_LIQUIDITY and then addTakePair. collectCallParameters (lines 413-423) encodes a decrease by zero and addTakePair."},
   {"url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Uniswap/sdks/main/sdks/v4-sdk/src/utils/v4Planner.ts", "supports": "The Actions enum (lines 30-66) has MINT_POSITION_FROM_DELTAS = 0x05 and CLEAR_OR_TAKE = 0x13 as comments only and has no entry for 0x17 or 0x18."},
   {"url": "https://forno.celo.org eth_call", "supports": "From owner 0xf18f712b760732cde4d1835673b98b2c7978b3a8 to PositionManager 0xf7965f3981e4d5bc383bfbcb61501763e9068ca9 at block 83,530,712, position 178: decrease then TAKE_PAIR reverts with 0x90bfb865 wrapping the G$ transfer, MINT_6909 reverts with 0x5cda29d7 and 0x17, sequences A and B return without error. Output in " + W + "raw/exit_42220_178.json."},
   {"url": "https://polygon-bor-rpc.publicnode.com eth_call", "supports": "From owner 0xb2d3f2324061c3a0acf0453f01a1045ebad1647b to PositionManager 0x1ec2ebf4f37e7363fdfe3551602425af0b3ceef9 at block 97,817,338, position 60652: same result with the ViciCoin transfer as the failing call. Output in " + W + "raw/exit_137_60652.json. Position 14963 in another ViciCoin pool exits with the normal sequence at block 97,817,667, which shows that the block depends on the amount and the allowance left that day (raw/exit_137_14963.json)."},
   {"url": "https://rpc.monad.xyz eth_call with state override", "supports": "Position 651334 at block 124,698,657 with the code of currency1 0xe7cd86e13ac4309349f30b3435a9d337750fc82d replaced by 0x5f5ffd: same pattern of reverts and the same two working sequences. Output in " + W + "raw/exitovr_143_651334.json. Arc position 333954 at block 32,722,324 gave the same result (raw/exitovr_5042_333954.json)."},
   {"url": "eth_call on the rpc endpoint of each network in state/networks.json (https://avalanche.drpc.org for Avalanche); results in " + W + "raw/posm_actions.json", "supports": "eth_call of modifyLiquidities with each action number 0 to 25 on the PositionManager of all 21 networks: actions 23 and 24 revert with UnsupportedAction on every network. The PositionManager has 23,877 bytes on 19 networks and 19,965 bytes on Elysium and HyperEVM."},
   {"url": "src/PoolManager.sol:322", "supports": "Core mints a claim against a positive delta without calling the token, so the missing route is in the periphery."}
  ],
  "evidence": "primary"
 }
]

